1
00:00:03,190 --> 00:00:04,940
Leonard, what time does your mom's plane get in?

2
00:00:04,940 --> 00:00:06,900
I don't know-- some time tomorrow morning.

3
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:08,250
Don't you want to know for sure?

4
00:00:08,250 --> 00:00:09,150
No need to.

5
00:00:09,150 --> 00:00:11,250
As soon as she flies into California airspace,

6
00:00:11,250 --> 00:00:13,980
I'll feel a disturbance in the Force.

7
00:00:14,470 --> 00:00:16,790
It's so nice both of your moms are coming in

8
00:00:16,790 --> 00:00:18,800
to see you guys get an award.

9
00:00:19,150 --> 00:00:21,820
Well, my mother's been there for every honor I've won

10
00:00:21,820 --> 00:00:23,310
since I beat out my twin sister

11
00:00:23,310 --> 00:00:26,420
for the "Did it on the potty" trophy.

12
00:00:26,880 --> 00:00:28,000
How does this look?

13
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,130
Aw, it's so nice. She's gonna love it.

14
00:00:30,130 --> 00:00:32,150
Sure, his mom gets roses.

15
00:00:32,150 --> 00:00:33,040
When I want them,

16
00:00:33,040 --> 00:00:36,880
they're a "bouquet of severed plant genitals."

17
00:00:37,450 --> 00:00:38,240
You act like I didn't get you

18
00:00:38,240 --> 00:00:41,250
that mushroom log on Valentine's Day.

19
00:00:41,680 --> 00:00:42,310
He's right.

20
00:00:42,310 --> 00:00:45,910
Roses die, but a moist rotting log will pump out mushrooms

21
00:00:45,910 --> 00:00:49,190
for two or three magical years.

22
00:00:49,190 --> 00:00:51,290
You know, your mom's never been too thrilled with our relationship.

23
00:00:51,290 --> 00:00:53,720
Maybe I should get her something so she warms up to me.

24
00:00:53,720 --> 00:00:55,390
If you could run out and get a PhD,

25
00:00:55,390 --> 00:00:57,410
that might make her like you.

26
00:00:57,820 --> 00:00:59,820
Really? It didn't work for you.

27
00:01:00,930 --> 00:01:02,870
Do you think the moms will get along?

28
00:01:02,870 --> 00:01:04,430
Uh, I don't know. They're pretty different.

29
00:01:04,430 --> 00:01:06,040
Maybe they'll be best friends.

30
00:01:06,040 --> 00:01:09,310
One of them is brilliant, one is sweet and simple.

31
00:01:09,310 --> 00:01:11,640
Sound familiar?

32
00:01:38,910 --> 00:01:42,530
Shelly, I'm so proud of you and Leonard for getting this award.

33
00:01:42,530 --> 00:01:43,650
Oh, thank you, Mother.

34
00:01:43,650 --> 00:01:45,760
I tried to read your paper, but it was very hard

35
00:01:45,760 --> 00:01:47,360
for me to understand.

36
00:01:47,360 --> 00:01:49,370
Oh, it's quite straightforward, actually.

37
00:01:49,370 --> 00:01:51,930
It describes a new model of the universe

38
00:01:51,930 --> 00:01:54,140
that conceptualizes it as the surface

39
00:01:54,140 --> 00:01:55,960
of an n-dimensional superfluid.

40
00:01:55,960 --> 00:01:56,920
Interesting.

41
00:01:56,920 --> 00:01:58,050
You can believe that,

42
00:01:58,050 --> 00:02:03,790
but God filling an ark with animals two-by-two is nonsense.

43
00:02:04,740 --> 00:02:08,150
What did they feed the lions, Mother?

44
00:02:08,850 --> 00:02:13,150
The floating bodies of drowned sinners, of course.

45
00:02:15,850 --> 00:02:19,790
Listen, Leonard's mom is a renowned psychiatrist

46
00:02:19,790 --> 00:02:21,160
and woman of science.

47
00:02:21,160 --> 00:02:24,040
Can you please keep the Bible babble to yourself

48
00:02:24,040 --> 00:02:25,690
while she's here?

49
00:02:25,690 --> 00:02:27,620
Are you ashamed of me?

50
00:02:27,620 --> 00:02:30,240
Of course not. I love you.

51
00:02:30,240 --> 00:02:36,280
I'm just embarrassed by the things you believe, do and say.

52
00:02:38,110 --> 00:02:40,980
Well, I love you, too.

53
00:02:41,290 --> 00:02:44,700
My little bowl of lion chow.

54
00:02:47,150 --> 00:02:49,360
So, have you and Penny set a wedding date?

55
00:02:49,360 --> 00:02:51,630
No, we're kind of taking it slow.

56
00:02:52,030 --> 00:02:53,480
I see.

57
00:02:56,890 --> 00:02:58,280
What does that mean?

58
00:02:58,280 --> 00:03:01,110
You've been on and off with this woman for seven years

59
00:03:01,110 --> 00:03:02,880
and engaged for one year.

60
00:03:02,880 --> 00:03:05,230
One has to wonder if there's a problem.

61
00:03:05,520 --> 00:03:08,640
Are you having satisfactory intercourse?

62
00:03:10,760 --> 00:03:12,780
Yes, Mother.

63
00:03:14,290 --> 00:03:17,490
Only satisfactory. I see.

64
00:03:19,390 --> 00:03:20,890
I change my answer.

65
00:03:20,890 --> 00:03:23,150
It-it's amazing. It's hot.

66
00:03:23,150 --> 00:03:25,960
We can barely keep our hands off each other.

67
00:03:26,690 --> 00:03:28,860
Seems odd to try and impress your mother

68
00:03:28,860 --> 00:03:31,570
with your sexual prowess.

69
00:03:32,160 --> 00:03:36,000
But then, you always did have that unresolved Oedipal complex.

70
00:03:36,750 --> 00:03:39,020
See, this right here, what you're doing,

71
00:03:39,020 --> 00:03:41,470
can you please not do that around Sheldon's mom?

72
00:03:41,470 --> 00:03:44,210
Why? Are you attracted to her, too?

73
00:03:44,890 --> 00:03:46,220
Of course not.

74
00:03:46,220 --> 00:03:49,480
She's-she's just a very sweet and God-fearing lady,

75
00:03:49,480 --> 00:03:51,490
and you have to be respectful of her beliefs.

76
00:03:51,490 --> 00:03:52,840
Leonard, I'm an adult.

77
00:03:52,840 --> 00:03:55,150
I know how to conduct myself around people

78
00:03:55,150 --> 00:03:57,090
from different walks of life.

79
00:03:57,090 --> 00:03:58,010
Thank you.

80
00:03:58,010 --> 00:03:58,990
Where is she from again?

81
00:03:58,990 --> 00:03:59,880
East Texas.

82
00:04:04,760 --> 00:04:07,190
Hey, look who's here.

83
00:04:07,190 --> 00:04:10,430
Oh, Dr. Hofstadter, it's so good to see you again.

84
00:04:10,430 --> 00:04:11,590
Likewise.

85
00:04:11,590 --> 00:04:14,050
I read your paper; it was very impressive.

86
00:04:14,050 --> 00:04:15,360
Oh, thank you.

87
00:04:15,360 --> 00:04:17,310
We just spent two hours in traffic.

88
00:04:17,310 --> 00:04:20,390
Did you think to mention to me that you liked our paper?

89
00:04:20,390 --> 00:04:22,710
Of course I did, but it's a mother's job

90
00:04:22,710 --> 00:04:24,680
to make sure her child's self-esteem

91
00:04:24,680 --> 00:04:28,240
is not dependent on anyone's approval.

92
00:04:28,890 --> 00:04:32,020
That's so sweet, you think I have self-esteem.

93
00:04:33,010 --> 00:04:35,690
Dr. Hofstadter, I want you to meet my mother, Mary.

94
00:04:35,690 --> 00:04:36,540
So nice to meet you.

95
00:04:36,540 --> 00:04:38,690
Nice to meet you, too. How was your flight?

96
00:04:38,690 --> 00:04:40,030
Very pleasant. And yours?

97
00:04:40,030 --> 00:04:42,060
Lovely. Almost as if someone--

98
00:04:42,060 --> 00:04:46,170
not saying who-- was watching over the plane.

99
00:04:47,540 --> 00:04:49,410
You're kidding, right?

100
00:04:50,780 --> 00:04:53,400
Subtle, Mom, real subtle.

101
00:05:00,020 --> 00:05:01,200
Stuart.

102
00:05:01,770 --> 00:05:03,080
Morning.

103
00:05:04,550 --> 00:05:06,040
We talked about this.

104
00:05:06,040 --> 00:05:07,260
I don't mind you still living here,

105
00:05:07,260 --> 00:05:08,830
but we got to have some rules.

106
00:05:08,830 --> 00:05:11,860
And rule number one is pants.

107
00:05:19,710 --> 00:05:21,650
You must be very proud of your son.

108
00:05:21,650 --> 00:05:23,040
Oh, yes.

109
00:05:23,040 --> 00:05:26,820
He recently argued a case before the Supreme Court.

110
00:05:28,230 --> 00:05:30,430
He did?

111
00:05:31,140 --> 00:05:33,600
Oh, you mean this son.

112
00:05:34,980 --> 00:05:37,450
Uh, sure, he's terrific.

113
00:05:37,920 --> 00:05:41,060
Uh, Beverly, would you like to see the math I worked out

114
00:05:41,060 --> 00:05:42,390
to support our hypothesis?

115
00:05:42,390 --> 00:05:43,820
Uh, you mean, my hypothesis.

116
00:05:43,820 --> 00:05:45,640
I hypothesized it all by myself.

117
00:05:45,640 --> 00:05:47,590
Calm down, dear.

118
00:05:48,010 --> 00:05:48,950
Mary, I'm curious.

119
00:05:48,950 --> 00:05:50,390
When did you first realize

120
00:05:50,390 --> 00:05:52,740
that your son had such a remarkable mind?

121
00:05:52,740 --> 00:05:54,720
Ooh, good question.

122
00:05:54,720 --> 00:05:58,840
Everyone loves stories about Sheldon Cooper, boy genius.

123
00:05:59,260 --> 00:06:01,210
Well, I would have to say when he was 13

124
00:06:01,210 --> 00:06:04,250
and tried to build a nuclear reactor in the tool shed.

125
00:06:04,250 --> 00:06:06,970
Ooh, this is a good one.

126
00:06:07,600 --> 00:06:09,450
Now, the first thing you have to know about Shelly is

127
00:06:09,450 --> 00:06:10,780
ever since he was a little boy,

128
00:06:10,780 --> 00:06:15,160
he was always concerned with the well-being of others.

129
00:06:17,500 --> 00:06:19,520
And he didn't think that it was fair

130
00:06:19,520 --> 00:06:21,310
for people to pay for electricity,

131
00:06:21,310 --> 00:06:24,710
so he was gonna power the entire town for free.

132
00:06:24,710 --> 00:06:26,130
Tell her about the uranium!

133
00:06:26,130 --> 00:06:27,360
Tell her about the uranium.

134
00:06:27,360 --> 00:06:28,280
Oh, well!

135
00:06:28,280 --> 00:06:30,210
Oh, this is adorable.

136
00:06:30,210 --> 00:06:33,980
When he arranged to get some yellowcake from Chad,

137
00:06:33,980 --> 00:06:35,970
I thought he was talking about Twinkies

138
00:06:35,970 --> 00:06:38,330
from one of his friends.

139
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:40,260
But I wasn't.

140
00:06:40,260 --> 00:06:42,800
'Cause I didn't have any friends.

141
00:06:43,860 --> 00:06:45,160
No.

142
00:06:45,580 --> 00:06:47,860
It turns out that this little scallywag was trying

143
00:06:47,860 --> 00:06:50,500
to use my Visa card to buy uranium

144
00:06:50,500 --> 00:06:55,870
from an African warlord in the country of Chad!

145
00:06:56,900 --> 00:06:58,790
Sounds like Sheldon was a handful.

146
00:06:58,790 --> 00:07:00,600
Oh, he was a handful.

147
00:07:00,600 --> 00:07:02,720
I was a handful.

148
00:07:03,670 --> 00:07:05,500
You still are.

149
00:07:09,570 --> 00:07:11,910
Uh, Mom, hey, tell Mary the story

150
00:07:11,910 --> 00:07:14,660
about how I made a Van de Graaff generator

151
00:07:14,660 --> 00:07:16,700
out of our vacuum cleaner.

152
00:07:16,700 --> 00:07:18,070
All right.

153
00:07:18,410 --> 00:07:20,850
He broke the vacuum cleaner.

154
00:07:26,790 --> 00:07:29,420
I mean, for a while, everything was vampires.

155
00:07:29,420 --> 00:07:30,980
Now it's all zombies.

156
00:07:30,980 --> 00:07:33,430
I wonder what the next monster fad will be.

157
00:07:33,430 --> 00:07:36,100
We haven't had a good invisible man in a while.

158
00:07:36,100 --> 00:07:39,840
Clearly, you've never seen me try to talk to a woman.

159
00:07:41,330 --> 00:07:42,410
Guys.

160
00:07:42,410 --> 00:07:44,460
In the time you've been sitting here playing video games,

161
00:07:44,460 --> 00:07:46,650
I got the car washed, picked up cleaning supplies

162
00:07:46,650 --> 00:07:48,200
and went to the bank.

163
00:07:48,200 --> 00:07:50,150
I put on pants.

164
00:07:52,040 --> 00:07:54,140
Kiss-ass.

165
00:07:56,160 --> 00:07:57,440
Okay, I don't know when I became

166
00:07:57,440 --> 00:07:59,080
the mother to three lazy teenagers,

167
00:07:59,080 --> 00:08:00,170
but it stops today.

168
00:08:00,170 --> 00:08:02,790
You guys are cleaning the kitchen, top to bottom.

169
00:08:02,790 --> 00:08:05,380
Hey, I don't even live here.

170
00:08:06,370 --> 00:08:09,500
Yes or no, do you have clothes in my laundry right now?

171
00:08:09,500 --> 00:08:11,880
I do.

172
00:08:11,880 --> 00:08:13,360
And some of it's wool,

173
00:08:13,360 --> 00:08:15,780
so dry flat if possible.

174
00:08:18,260 --> 00:08:22,670
Oh, and here's a picture of me receiving my bachelor of science degree.

175
00:08:22,670 --> 00:08:24,400
You don't look very happy.

176
00:08:24,400 --> 00:08:27,510
Well, I had just begun puberty.

177
00:08:28,780 --> 00:08:30,820
It was figuratively and literally

178
00:08:30,820 --> 00:08:34,490
one of the hairiest moments of my life.

179
00:08:34,490 --> 00:08:36,830
Shelly does not like change.

180
00:08:36,830 --> 00:08:37,770
Oh, true.

181
00:08:37,770 --> 00:08:40,000
But all the clenching in the world will not keep

182
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:42,760
testicles in your abdomen.

183
00:08:44,360 --> 00:08:46,430
Hey, sorry, got caught up at work.

184
00:08:46,430 --> 00:08:48,200
- Hi, Beverly! - Hello.

185
00:08:48,420 --> 00:08:50,350
Oh, okay.

186
00:08:51,240 --> 00:08:52,620
Sorry, I forgot.

187
00:08:52,620 --> 00:08:53,840
You remember my mother.

188
00:08:53,840 --> 00:08:55,180
Oh, yes. Hi, Mary!

189
00:08:55,180 --> 00:08:57,190
Good to see you again, dear.

190
00:08:57,190 --> 00:08:59,850
Ah, yeah, now that's what I'm talking about.

191
00:09:00,610 --> 00:09:03,240
So, Mom, you haven't seen Penny since we got engaged.

192
00:09:03,240 --> 00:09:05,100
Oh, yeah, let me show you the ring.

193
00:09:05,100 --> 00:09:06,480
Oh, lovely.

194
00:09:06,480 --> 00:09:08,260
Must have been very expensive.

195
00:09:08,260 --> 00:09:09,420
Oh, no, not at all.

196
00:09:09,420 --> 00:09:11,710
No, we, uh, found a place online

197
00:09:11,710 --> 00:09:15,630
that, uh, repurposes diamond drill bits.

198
00:09:17,010 --> 00:09:19,180
We did not. That's not true.

199
00:09:19,810 --> 00:09:22,130
Can I speak to you alone for a second?

200
00:09:22,130 --> 00:09:23,320
Oh, sure.

201
00:09:23,710 --> 00:09:25,230
It came from Tiffany's.

202
00:09:25,930 --> 00:09:27,050
You mean the box, right?

203
00:09:27,050 --> 00:09:28,660
Keep walking!

204
00:09:31,430 --> 00:09:34,840
Really doesn't matter to me how much he spent on the ring.

205
00:09:35,230 --> 00:09:37,090
I think.

206
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:39,850
Did I misspeak about the ring?

207
00:09:39,850 --> 00:09:42,300
Yes, and we'll get back to that.

208
00:09:42,300 --> 00:09:44,130
But, uh, even with your mother here,

209
00:09:44,130 --> 00:09:47,010
you are deliberately hogging all the attention from my mom.

210
00:09:47,010 --> 00:09:49,050
You're like one of those elephant seal pups

211
00:09:49,050 --> 00:09:51,830
that steals the milk from two mothers!

212
00:09:52,730 --> 00:09:54,670
Do you mean what marine biologists

213
00:09:54,670 --> 00:09:56,690
refer to as "super weaning"?

214
00:09:56,690 --> 00:09:59,780
Yes, you are a super weaner!

215
00:10:02,820 --> 00:10:05,000
Well, now I have to correct you.

216
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:08,110
A-As a bit of an elephant seal buff,

217
00:10:08,110 --> 00:10:09,900
the more accurate comparison

218
00:10:09,900 --> 00:10:11,690
would be when two mother seals

219
00:10:11,690 --> 00:10:13,830
actively seek to nourish the same pup.

220
00:10:13,830 --> 00:10:16,220
So I believe the term you're looking for

221
00:10:16,220 --> 00:10:18,910
is a double mother suckler.

222
00:10:21,020 --> 00:10:21,840
Yeah, you're right.

223
00:10:21,840 --> 00:10:23,520
That is the term I'm looking for.

224
00:10:23,520 --> 00:10:26,990
You are a dirty double mother suckler!

225
00:10:29,230 --> 00:10:32,190
Okay, well, now that we have the terminology straightened out.

226
00:10:32,190 --> 00:10:34,680
How dare you!

227
00:10:35,860 --> 00:10:37,070
We're not in a rush.

228
00:10:37,070 --> 00:10:38,620
We'll set a date when the time is right.

229
00:10:38,620 --> 00:10:40,080
It doesn't matter, sweetie.

230
00:10:40,080 --> 00:10:41,700
The moment a man lays with a woman,

231
00:10:41,700 --> 00:10:44,240
they are married in the eyes of the Lord.

232
00:10:52,640 --> 00:10:54,790
The bible is "uch" to you?

233
00:10:54,790 --> 00:10:56,670
No, I'm sorry. That was inappropriate.

234
00:10:56,670 --> 00:10:58,060
As a psychiatrist,

235
00:10:58,060 --> 00:11:02,730
I know how important people's superstitions can be to them.

236
00:11:04,230 --> 00:11:06,260
You want to talk about superstitions?

237
00:11:06,260 --> 00:11:08,180
Sheldon sent me the books you wrote--

238
00:11:08,180 --> 00:11:10,790
all that nonsense about superegos and ids.

239
00:11:10,790 --> 00:11:14,530
What bull dropped that on the barn floor?

240
00:11:14,630 --> 00:11:16,910
His name is Sigmund Freud.

241
00:11:16,910 --> 00:11:18,090
Hey, look at that!

242
00:11:18,090 --> 00:11:21,330
You both believe in Jewish bearded guys.

243
00:11:22,690 --> 00:11:24,460
Stay out of this.

244
00:11:25,730 --> 00:11:27,930
At least the bearded man that I believe in

245
00:11:27,930 --> 00:11:29,740
preaches love and compassion.

246
00:11:29,740 --> 00:11:31,310
All yours talks about is

247
00:11:31,310 --> 00:11:32,790
why you hold in your poop

248
00:11:32,790 --> 00:11:36,060
and want to crawl back inside your mama.

249
00:11:38,490 --> 00:11:40,070
It's fascinating.

250
00:11:40,070 --> 00:11:42,300
How can someone as enlightened as Sheldon

251
00:11:42,300 --> 00:11:45,030
come from someone like you?

252
00:11:46,070 --> 00:11:47,210
I know the answer.

253
00:11:47,210 --> 00:11:49,210
You're not gonna like it.

254
00:11:49,830 --> 00:11:50,700
Try me.

255
00:11:50,700 --> 00:11:53,760
When I was pregnant with Shelly, I was driving to church,

256
00:11:53,760 --> 00:11:55,270
and I was praying to the Lord

257
00:11:55,270 --> 00:11:59,120
to give me a son smarter than his dumb-ass daddy.

258
00:11:59,500 --> 00:12:03,140
And I looked over and I saw a Jesus bobblehead

259
00:12:03,140 --> 00:12:07,520
in the Subaru next to me nodding yes.

260
00:12:13,370 --> 00:12:14,790
What is that supposed to mean?

261
00:12:14,790 --> 00:12:15,790
It means...

262
00:12:15,790 --> 00:12:18,860
I can't believe we're having this conversation.

263
00:12:18,860 --> 00:12:20,360
Well, do it some more.

264
00:12:20,360 --> 00:12:23,800
Maybe you can knock some sense into yourself.

265
00:12:23,800 --> 00:12:26,020
I hope we all stops hitting ourselves

266
00:12:26,020 --> 00:12:27,560
and talk about something safe, you know,

267
00:12:27,560 --> 00:12:31,260
like shoes or how cute little Chinese babies are.

268
00:12:31,260 --> 00:12:33,720
Maybe it is not my fault that your mother likes me

269
00:12:33,720 --> 00:12:34,940
better than she likes you!

270
00:12:34,940 --> 00:12:35,720
Oh, don't flatter yourself!

271
00:12:35,720 --> 00:12:38,590
She likes everybody better than she likes me!

272
00:12:45,250 --> 00:12:46,940
How old is this Jell-O?

273
00:12:46,940 --> 00:12:50,990
Well, it's carrots, so gonna say very.

274
00:12:52,600 --> 00:12:54,940
Sorry we have to do this.

275
00:12:54,940 --> 00:12:56,220
Bernadette's not wrong.

276
00:12:56,220 --> 00:12:57,940
She does work hard around here.

277
00:12:57,940 --> 00:12:58,980
Yeah, maybe it's a good thing

278
00:12:58,980 --> 00:13:00,920
if she stops babying you so much.

279
00:13:00,920 --> 00:13:02,830
She doesn't baby me.

280
00:13:02,830 --> 00:13:05,910
I saw her pull you home in a wagon.

281
00:13:06,980 --> 00:13:07,780
For your information,

282
00:13:07,780 --> 00:13:10,910
I twisted my ankle chasing the ice cream truck.

283
00:13:11,640 --> 00:13:12,950
Face it, dude,

284
00:13:12,950 --> 00:13:15,340
Bernadette treats you the same way your mother used to,

285
00:13:15,340 --> 00:13:18,540
and that was not a healthy relationship.

286
00:13:20,130 --> 00:13:21,300
You're right.

287
00:13:21,870 --> 00:13:23,410
It's time for me

288
00:13:23,410 --> 00:13:26,930
to act like an adult in this marriage.

289
00:13:26,930 --> 00:13:32,160
Starting with my husbandly duty of taking out the trash.

290
00:13:37,450 --> 00:13:39,700
Bernie, I made a mess!

291
00:13:43,170 --> 00:13:46,110
I'm terribly sorry that I upset your mother.

292
00:13:46,110 --> 00:13:48,650
Oh, it's all right. She'll forgive you.

293
00:13:48,650 --> 00:13:51,820
She has to or she goes to hell.

294
00:13:54,340 --> 00:13:55,890
I can't help but notice

295
00:13:55,890 --> 00:13:58,590
how her unconditional love for you

296
00:13:58,590 --> 00:14:02,540
is diametrically opposed to my own parenting strategies.

297
00:14:02,540 --> 00:14:05,360
Well, you doled out affection

298
00:14:05,360 --> 00:14:07,960
as a reward for achievement--

299
00:14:07,960 --> 00:14:09,930
a proven way to raise a child.

300
00:14:09,930 --> 00:14:12,820
Or train a rat.

301
00:14:12,820 --> 00:14:15,130
But look how well you turned out.

302
00:14:15,130 --> 00:14:18,870
I'd feign modesty at this point, but who would believe me?

303
00:14:18,870 --> 00:14:20,970
Still, you need to consider

304
00:14:20,970 --> 00:14:23,850
how successful Leonard's brother and sister are.

305
00:14:23,850 --> 00:14:24,860
I suppose.

306
00:14:24,860 --> 00:14:28,730
While my brother and sister are mouth-breathing idiots.

307
00:14:29,810 --> 00:14:32,190
Do you suppose you would've flourished more

308
00:14:32,190 --> 00:14:34,750
in a reward-based environment?

309
00:14:35,050 --> 00:14:36,370
Perhaps.

310
00:14:36,370 --> 00:14:37,750
But my mom made me spaghetti

311
00:14:37,750 --> 00:14:40,180
with chopped-up hot dogs whenever I wanted,

312
00:14:40,180 --> 00:14:42,520
so who cares?

313
00:14:44,440 --> 00:14:46,860
Not once did my mother ever give me any love

314
00:14:46,860 --> 00:14:49,190
or affection for just being myself;

315
00:14:49,190 --> 00:14:50,420
I always had to earn it.

316
00:14:50,420 --> 00:14:53,620
Oh, Leonard, I'm sure she loves you very much.

317
00:14:53,620 --> 00:14:57,450
In her own cold godless way.

318
00:14:58,680 --> 00:15:01,290
Yeah, and you certainly don't have to earn my love.

319
00:15:01,290 --> 00:15:02,160
Thank you.

320
00:15:02,160 --> 00:15:03,380
Of course, you already knew that

321
00:15:03,380 --> 00:15:06,970
when you bought me this princess-cut drill bit.

322
00:15:07,750 --> 00:15:08,970
That's not what it is.

323
00:15:08,970 --> 00:15:11,330
I know, I know.

324
00:15:14,550 --> 00:15:16,190
When your mom gets back, I'm gonna need

325
00:15:16,190 --> 00:15:18,320
to apologize for the way I spoke to her.

326
00:15:18,320 --> 00:15:20,320
Well, come on now, she did kind of start it.

327
00:15:20,320 --> 00:15:23,650
Doesn't matter; a good Christian would've turned the other cheek.

328
00:15:23,650 --> 00:15:24,350
On the other hand,

329
00:15:24,350 --> 00:15:26,850
a good Texan would've shot her, so...

330
00:15:29,310 --> 00:15:31,940
I just kind of split the difference.

331
00:15:33,090 --> 00:15:35,790
Hey, who's in the mood for spaghetti and hot dogs?

332
00:15:35,790 --> 00:15:36,670
Oh, me!

333
00:15:36,670 --> 00:15:37,470
Yeah, me, too!

334
00:15:37,470 --> 00:15:38,640
Coming up.

335
00:15:39,870 --> 00:15:42,520
I don't really feel I deserve it.

336
00:15:45,390 --> 00:15:46,700
That was a big sticky mess,

337
00:15:46,700 --> 00:15:48,480
but... I think I got it.

338
00:15:48,480 --> 00:15:49,570
Looks good.

339
00:15:50,930 --> 00:15:51,560
Look at that.

340
00:15:51,560 --> 00:15:53,620
You cleaned it up all by yourself.

341
00:15:53,950 --> 00:15:56,800
Yes, I cleaned it up all by myself.

342
00:15:56,800 --> 00:15:58,750
Honestly, I don't know why you complain so...

343
00:16:00,740 --> 00:16:02,640
Okay, maybe I missed one spot.

344
00:16:09,540 --> 00:16:11,540
Just leave.

345
00:16:13,420 --> 00:16:16,180
I'm so glad that you and I were able to bury the hatchet.

346
00:16:16,180 --> 00:16:17,010
Me, too.

347
00:16:17,010 --> 00:16:19,470
And I respect your right to your beliefs.

348
00:16:19,470 --> 00:16:21,670
And I will pray for you.

349
00:16:24,190 --> 00:16:25,970
Okay, Mom, let's get you back to your hotel

350
00:16:25,970 --> 00:16:27,850
before anyone says anything else.

351
00:16:27,850 --> 00:16:29,250
One moment.

352
00:16:29,250 --> 00:16:31,400
There's something I need to say to you.

353
00:16:31,400 --> 00:16:33,540
Oh, really? That's too bad.

354
00:16:34,350 --> 00:16:37,980
Leonard, I always made you earn my affection,

355
00:16:37,980 --> 00:16:39,930
but today I realize that

356
00:16:39,930 --> 00:16:42,520
there's more than one way to raise a child.

357
00:16:42,520 --> 00:16:44,640
I taught her that!

358
00:16:45,650 --> 00:16:46,720
Therefore, I would like

359
00:16:46,720 --> 00:16:50,400
to initiate a new protocol wherein I...

360
00:16:50,400 --> 00:16:53,940
shower you with unconditional love.

361
00:16:56,720 --> 00:16:58,310
When does that start?

362
00:16:58,950 --> 00:17:00,550
So needy.

363
00:17:05,120 --> 00:17:06,950
Come to Mommy.

364
00:17:09,010 --> 00:17:11,020
It's okay, go ahead.

365
00:17:18,430 --> 00:17:20,430
Oh, my son.

366
00:17:22,830 --> 00:17:24,840
Oh, my mother.

367
00:17:25,810 --> 00:17:27,790
Oh, my God.

368
00:17:52,180 --> 00:17:54,000
* It's a hard-knock life *

369
00:17:56,350 --> 00:17:59,600
* It's the hard-knock life for us *

370
00:17:59,600 --> 00:18:02,940
* It's the hard-knock life for us *

371
00:18:02,940 --> 00:18:06,030
* 'Stead of treated, we get tricked *

372
00:18:06,030 --> 00:18:09,430
* 'Stead of kisses, we get kicked *

373
00:18:09,430 --> 00:18:11,750
* It's the hard-knock life *

374
00:18:11,750 --> 00:18:15,260
* Got no folks to speak of so *

375
00:18:15,260 --> 00:18:18,460
* It's the hard-knock row we hoe *

376
00:18:18,460 --> 00:18:21,800
* Cotton blankets... 'stead of wool *

377
00:18:21,800 --> 00:18:24,690
* Empty bellies... 'stead of full *

378
00:18:24,690 --> 00:18:26,650
* It's a hard-knock life. *

